# Wave 42 §P item 3 — W16: "i played worldbreaker and it went on the stack.
# but the effect that i'm choosing was never explained to me. the decision
# box should pop up for things like this." The real card is World Breaker
# (`forge-gui/res/cardsfolder/w/world_breaker.txt`): "When you cast this
# spell, exile target artifact, enchantment, or land" — a SpellCast trigger,
# fired the instant the spell is cast (before it even resolves), targeting
# any artifact/enchantment/LAND on either battlefield — `ValidTgts$
# Artifact,Enchantment,Land` has no `+Other`/opponent restriction, so every
# land on the table, seat 0's own included, is a legal target.
#
# Seat 0 (human) holds World Breaker (`{6}{G}`) and seven untapped lands —
# one Forest for the pip, six Mountains for the generic — so casting it
# leaves none spare for anything else. Seat 1 has one Mountain of its own,
# so there are EIGHT total legal targets (every land on the table): enough
# that Forge cannot auto-pick a lone one, and must actually ask.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=World Breaker
humanbattlefield=Forest;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=Mountain
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
